     1,
     "Hi, all<div><br></div><div>I have a data frame from a QTL analysis in plant with four columns: Markers, Chromosome, Genetic Map (in centimorgan) and o LOD score values. I would like to plot this value in a graph like the graph attached.  </div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"256\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:192pt\">\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:48pt\">\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:48pt\">marker</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">chr</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">gen_map</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">LOD</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">rs1</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1</td>\n  <td>0</td>\n  <td>14.740</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">rs1</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1</td>\n  <td>0.9</td>\n  <td>14.350</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">rs3</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1</td>\n  <td>3.7</td>\n  <td>11.806</td>\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>Are there someone that can help me, please?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you so much.</div><div><br></div><div>Rodrigo</div><div><br></div><div> </div>"
    ]
   ]
